<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BPI H1 cons net up 37 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BPI H1 cons net up 37 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to June 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net 11.3 vs 8.3</p>
<p>Cash flow before tax 20.5 vs 13.9</p>
<p>Note - Banco Portugues de Investimento is company name.  </p>
<p>    Banking income		   55.2   vs    26.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   13.6   vs     9.4</p>
<p>    Financial margin		 37.2   vs    16.7</p>
<p>    Commissions and other income 15.0   vs     4.7</p>
<p>    Structural costs		 35.2   vs    14.5</p>
<p>    Total assets		  2,999.0   vs 2,889.0</p>
<p>    Client loans		  1,211.0   vs 1,159.0</p>
<p>Deposits and other client</p>
<p>    funds			   2,587.0   vs 2,357.0</p>
<p>Percentage cover of loans</p>
<p>    over 90 days overdue     129 pct    vs 106 pct</p>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento said that the results were not directly comparable with the first half of 1996 because of the purchase of Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior.</p>
<p>It noted that the weight commission income in its total earnings from banking had risen to 27 percent in the period from 18 percent in the same period last year.</p>
<p>($1=184 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
